{"id": "section-body-27100", "title": "Psychiatric Disorders in Pregnancy", "chapterId": "chapter-twenty-three", "blocks": [{"id": "body-27100", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading2", "text": "Psychiatric Disorders in Pregnancy", "runs": [{"text": "Psychiatric"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Disorders"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Pregnancy"}], "level": 2, "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "359"}}, {"id": "body-27101", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "In some women, pregnancy and motherhood increase their vulnerability to psychiatric conditions such as depression, anxiety disorders, eating disorders, panic disorder, bipolar illness, and psychoses. These conditions are often underdiagnosed because they are attributed to pregnancy- related changes in maternal temperament or physiology. In addition, such conditions are often undertreated because of concerns about potential harmful effects of medication.", "runs": [{"text": "In some women, pregnancy and motherhood increase their vulnerability to psychiatric conditions such as depression, anxiety disorders,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "eating"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "disorders,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "panic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "disorder,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "bipolar"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "illness,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "psychoses."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "These"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "conditions"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "often"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "underdiagnosed"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "because they"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "attributed"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pregnancy-"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "related"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "changes"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "maternal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "temperament"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "physiology."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "In"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "addition,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "such"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "conditions"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "often undertreated because of concerns about potential harmful effects of medication."}]}, {"id": "body-27102", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Depression", "runs": [{"text": "Depression"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "341"}}, {"id": "body-27103", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Several risk factors and psychosocial correlates have been identified as contributing to depression during pregnancy, like; Previous history of depression, discontinuation of medication(s) by a woman who has a history of depression, a previous history of postpartum depression, and a family history of depression.", "runs": [{"text": "Several risk factors and psychosocial correlates have been identified as contributing to depression during pregnancy, like; Previous"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "history"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "depression,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "discontinuation"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "medication(s)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "woman"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "who"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "has"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "history"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "depression,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "previous"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "history of postpartum depression, and a family history of depression."}]}, {"id": "body-27105", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Several key psychosocial correlates may also contribute to depression during pregnancy: a negative attitude toward the pregnancy, a lack of social support, maternal stress associated with negative life events, and a partner or family member who is unhappy about the pregnancy. The relationship between maternal depression and early childhood problems may be part of a sequence that starts with depressive symptoms during pregnancy.", "runs": [{"text": "Several key psychosocial correlates may also contribute to depression during pregnancy: a negative attitude toward the pregnancy,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a lack of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "social"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "support,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "maternal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "stress associated with negative life events,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and a partner"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "family member"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "who is unhappy about the pregnancy. The relationship between maternal depression and early childhood problems may be part of a sequence that starts with depressive symptoms during pregnancy."}]}, {"id": "body-27107", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Non-Pharmacological Management", "runs": [{"text": "Non-Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-27108", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Psychotherapies", "runs": [{"text": "Psychotherapies"}]}, {"id": "body-27109", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Cognitive behavioral therapy", "runs": [{"text": "Cognitive"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "behavioral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "therapy"}], "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "341"}}, {"id": "body-27110", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Interpersonal psychotherapy", "runs": [{"text": "Interpersonal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "psychotherapy"}], "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "341"}}, {"id": "body-27111", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Education and support are also important, particularly as pregnancy is a unique experience for women, some of whom may not know what to expect.", "runs": [{"text": "Education"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "support"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "also"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "important,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "particularly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "as"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pregnancy"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "unique"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "experience"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "women,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "some"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "whom may not know what to expect."}], "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "341"}}, {"id": "body-27112", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Pharmacological Management", "runs": [{"text": "Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-27113", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "A: amitriptyline, (PO), 12.5–75 mg 24hourly at night, increase gradually to a maximum of 150 mg daily. {Elderly: Initially 12.5– 50 mg. Max. 75mg)", "runs": [{"text": "A:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "amitriptyline,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO),"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "12.5–75"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "24hourly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "at"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "night,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "increase"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "gradually"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "maximum"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "150"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "daily."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "{Elderly:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Initially"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "12.5– 50 mg. Max. 75mg)"}]}, {"id": "body-27114", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "OR", "runs": [{"text": "OR"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-27115", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "D: citalopram (PO) ,10-60mg 24hourly morning or evening and symptoms should be monitored, and medication to be tapered", "runs": [{"text": "D:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "citalopram"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": ",10-60mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "24hourly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "morning"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "evening"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "symptoms"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "should"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "monitored,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "medication"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tapered"}]}, {"id": "body-27116", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "OR", "runs": [{"text": "OR"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-27117", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "S: fluoxetine (PO) 20-60mg 24hourly (morning)", "runs": [{"text": "S:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "fluoxetine"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "20-60mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "24hourly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(morning)"}]}, {"id": "body-27118", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "OR", "runs": [{"text": "OR"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-27119", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "S: escitalopram (PO) 10-20 mg nocte (titrating according to individual response)", "runs": [{"text": "S:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "escitalopram"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "10-20"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "nocte"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(titrating"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "according"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "individual"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "response)"}]}, {"id": "body-27120-textbox1-00001", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Normal", "text": "Note:", "runs": [{"text": "Note:", "bold": true}]}, {"id": "body-27120-textbox1-00002", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Full disclosure of both the risk and benefits of various antidepressant medications should be made to the patient and, if possible, her partner prior to starting any Pharmacological management.", "runs": [{"text": "Full"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "disclosure"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "both"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "risk"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "benefits"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "various"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "antidepressant"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "medications"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "should"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "made"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patient"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and, if possible, her partner prior to starting any Pharmacological management."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "340"}}, {"id": "body-27120-textbox1-00003", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Low doses of antidepressants should be considered when initiating medication.", "runs": [{"text": "Low"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "doses"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "antidepressants"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "should"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "considered"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "when"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "initiating"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "medication."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "340"}}, {"id": "body-27122", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Panic Disorder", "runs": [{"text": "Panic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Disorder"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "339"}}, {"id": "body-27123", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Some women may experience first-onset panic disorder during pregnancy. Women presenting with panic attacks for the first time should be screened for thyroid disorder. The correlation between plasma levels of cortisol in the mother and in the fetus may have implications for the developing fetal brain.", "runs": [{"text": "Some women may experience first-onset panic disorder during pregnancy. Women presenting with panic attacks for the first time should be screened for thyroid disorder. The correlation between plasma levels of cortisol in the mother and in the fetus may have implications for the developing fetal brain."}]}, {"id": "body-27125", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Non-Pharmacological management", "runs": [{"text": "Non-Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-27126", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Cognitive behavioral therapy", "runs": [{"text": "Cognitive"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "behavioral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "therapy"}], "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "339"}}, {"id": "body-27127", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Supportive psychotherapy", "runs": [{"text": "Supportive"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "psychotherapy"}], "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "339"}}, {"id": "body-27128", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Relaxation techniques", "runs": [{"text": "Relaxation"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "techniques"}], "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "339"}}, {"id": "body-27129", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Sleep hygiene", "runs": [{"text": "Sleep"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hygiene"}], "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "339"}}, {"id": "body-27130", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Dietary counseling", "runs": [{"text": "Dietary"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "counseling"}], "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "339"}}, {"id": "body-27132", "type": "heading"